# Turborepo Monorepo

Use this rule when changing workspace configuration, CI, Docker, or commands after the Turborepo migration.

## Workspace Layout

- Frontend app: `apps/frontend`
- Backend app: `apps/backend`
- Future shared packages: `packages/*`
- Root workspace files: `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `turbo.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`

## Package Manager

- Use pnpm from the repository root.
- Enable Corepack before installing in fresh environments:
  ```bash
  corepack enable
  pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
  ```
- Do not add new app-level lockfiles. The canonical lockfile is the root `pnpm-lock.yaml`.

## Commands

- All apps: `pnpm build`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check-types`, `pnpm test`
- Frontend only: `pnpm turbo run build --filter=@repo/frontend`
- Backend only: `pnpm turbo run build --filter=@repo/backend`
- Frontend dev: `pnpm turbo run dev --filter=@repo/frontend`
- Backend dev: `pnpm turbo run develop --filter=@repo/backend`

## Next.js 16

- Use the ESLint CLI directly. Do not use `next lint`; it was removed in Next.js 16.
- The frontend uses standalone output. In this monorepo, keep `outputFileTracingRoot` pointed at the repository root when runtime tracing needs files outside `apps/frontend`.

## Docker And CI

- Docker image builds that depend on the workspace should use the repository root as context and app Dockerfiles by path:
  - `apps/frontend/main.Dockerfile`
  - `apps/frontend/dev.Dockerfile`
  - `apps/backend/main.Dockerfile`
  - `apps/backend/dev.Dockerfile`
- Preserve remote deployment directories such as `/opt/infinity/frontend` and `/opt/infinity/backend` unless an infrastructure task explicitly changes them.
- Do not copy or cache Strapi runtime data:
  - `apps/backend/public/uploads/**`
  - `apps/backend/.tmp/**`
  - local SQLite files
  - `.env` files
